<x-public-layout title="Privacy Policy">
<article class="reference-container ats-guide policy-document">
<header class="ats-guide-intro"><span class="reference-eyebrow">HOW YOUR INFORMATION IS HANDLED</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p class="policy-status">Effective date: 22 October 2026</p><p><strong>atscvdetector</strong> operates <strong>atscvdetector.com</strong> and determines why and how personal information is processed for this service. This policy covers our accounts, CV builder, matching tools, optional rewriting and support. Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a> with “Privacy request” in the subject for questions or requests.</p></header>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>1. Information we process</h2><ul class="ats-guide-checklist"><li><strong>Account details:</strong> name, email address, hashed password where used, verification details and account records.</li><li><strong>Google sign-in:</strong> if selected, your Google identifier, name, email address and verification status. This flow does not request Gmail messages, contacts or Drive files. We do not receive your Google password.</li><li><strong>Career information:</strong> documents, extracted text, contact details, employment and education history, skills, references, job descriptions, edits and generated drafts you supply or request.</li><li><strong>Saved work and sessions:</strong> builder drafts, saved CV versions and information needed to continue a workflow. You can start a builder draft without an account. Sign in and verify your email to save a CV to your account or download it.</li><li><strong>Technical records:</strong> IP addresses, browser or device information, session identifiers, request times and diagnostic or security records where generated by the application or hosting systems.</li><li><strong>Support messages:</strong> your email, message and any attachments you send. </li><li><strong>Payments:</strong> selected plans or credit packs, payment providers, transaction references, amounts, currencies, payment and renewal status, and related credit allocations. Card entry is handled by the selected payment provider; full card details are not stored in your account here.</li></ul></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>2. Why we use information</h2><p>We use it to create and secure accounts, verify emails, recover access, build and export CVs, compare text with job descriptions, provide requested rewriting, save your work and answer enquiries. Necessary processing also prevents abuse, diagnoses faults and meets applicable obligations.</p><p>Depending on the activity and applicable law, processing grounds include providing a requested service or performing a contract, consent where required, compliance with legal obligations and legitimate operational or security interests where permitted and balanced against your rights. Agreeing to terms is not consent to every possible use of your data.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>3. Optional external AI processing</h2><p>Match scores are calculated within our application. When you request AI analysis or rewriting, relevant CV text, the job description, confirmed skills and analysis details are sent to OpenAI (or the configured rewriting provider). Returned content may be held in your session and saved when you choose to continue into the builder.</p><p>External providers may process information in countries with different privacy laws from your own. A provider's applicable terms govern its own handling, security and retention. Job-to-CV ATS Detector includes AI analysis and CV revamping uses OpenAI through its API. CV text may include contact or referee details if you leave them in the submitted document. OpenAI states that API data is not used for training by default unless the API customer opts in. Default abuse-monitoring logs may retain content for up to 30 days, subject to exceptions, and other storage depends on the feature and account configuration. We do not promise zero retention by an external provider. See <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI's API data controls</a> for its current handling. Ask support if those details are unclear. You can use manual editing and the basic ATS Checker instead of requesting AI processing.</p><p>Remove unnecessary sensitive data, identity numbers, financial details and third-party contacts. Manual CV editing and the basic ATS Checker do not request AI rewriting. Job-to-CV ATS Detector includes AI analysis, and the CV revamp uses the configured AI provider. Withdrawing consent stops future consent-based processing but cannot reverse a completed request.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>4. Who may receive information</h2><p>Hosting and infrastructure suppliers, email delivery providers, your selected sign-in provider, AI providers for requested functions and authorised support personnel may process information needed for their roles, under appropriate arrangements. When separate document processing is enabled, a secured document-processing host receives uploaded PDF bytes to extract text, or generated CV HTML to create a requested PDF or Word download. This can include contact and referee information present in the CV. The worker does not use that content for AI training and is configured to delete temporary documents after processing; crashes, hosting buffers and provider backups can affect retention. We review the selected hosting arrangements before activation. Public pages also load Google-hosted fonts; your browser sends connection information such as your IP address to Google for that request.</p><p>We do not sell CVs, provide a public CV directory or send your CV to employers as part of these tools. Information may be disclosed when lawfully required, to address security incidents or protect legal rights, or during a business transfer with appropriate safeguards and required notice. Advertising or unrelated marketing use would need a separate lawful basis and clear notice.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>5. Cookies and sessions</h2><p>Essential cookies and server-side sessions maintain sign-in, protect forms and connect editing steps. Blocking or deleting them can sign you out, interrupt a workflow or make an unsaved draft unavailable. A sign-in provider can separately use cookies on its own service.</p><p>The current application does not include advertising trackers or third-party behavioural analytics. If optional tracking is introduced, we will explain it and seek consent where required before enabling it.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>6. Storage and retention</h2><p>This is an account-based service. Saved CV content is stored so you can reopen and edit it. Uploaded files, extracted text, drafts and generated documents may also exist in temporary storage or sessions during processing. Closing a browser tab does not guarantee erasure. We do not describe all processing as storage-free or immediately deleted.</p><p>We retain account information and saved content while needed to provide your account, unless you request deletion or another lawful retention reason applies. Sessions, temporary files, logs and support records serve different purposes and may remain for different periods.</p><p>On a verified deletion request, we remove or anonymise information no longer needed, subject to lawful exceptions. Disputes, security incidents, statutory obligations and restricted backups may justify limited retention for those purposes. Contact support for information about retention periods and backup handling relevant to your request.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>7. Security and international processing</h2><p>The application uses password hashing, authenticated access, document ownership checks and request protections. No website or transmission method guarantees absolute security. Protect your device and email account, and never disclose credentials to support.</p><p>Providers may process data in countries with different privacy laws. Applicable requirements for lawful international transfers and appropriate safeguards remain applicable. We will provide personal data breach notifications where law requires them. This policy is not a claim of regulatory certification or a guarantee against incidents.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>8. Your choices and rights</h2><p>Depending on applicable law and exceptions, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection to certain processing, withdrawal of consent and portability where provided by law. You can update your name and password in your profile. Your account email cannot be changed through Settings; contact support for account access assistance. Password accounts can request deletion there; if Google sign-in prevents password confirmation, contact support for verified deletion assistance.</p><p>Email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>, describing your request and account. We may need proportionate identity verification. Do not send identity documents unless securely requested. We will respond within the legally required period and explain any permitted refusal or extension.</p><p>You may complain directly to a competent privacy regulator without completing our support process first.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>9. Children and third parties</h2><p>Account services are intended for adults aged 18 or over. If a child's information has been submitted, contact us so we can investigate and take appropriate action. Include referees' or other people's information only with a lawful basis and only where necessary.</p></section>

<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>10. Automated assessments and your decisions</h2><p>Our tools analyse readable structure and how a CV aligns with detected job requirements. Our application calculates matching measures and uses AI assistance for analysis and rewriting. Results can be incomplete or incorrect. We do not make hiring decisions, automatically reject candidates, submit applications or send your results to employers through these tools.</p><p>Check all recommendations before using them, particularly qualifications, licences, employment dates, experience and skill claims. You decide whether to accept generated wording. A score is not an employer's actual ATS score or a guarantee of selection.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>11. Payment providers and usage records</h2><p>Paystack or Paynow processes payment information within its own payment flow when available at checkout. The provider may return limited payment-method metadata, transaction identifiers and subscription status. Its own privacy notice applies. We do not ask for your banking password, PIN or card security code by email.</p><p>Credit records include allocations, reservations, deductions, reversals and balances. We use payment and usage records to verify delivery, correct failed requests, prevent duplicate benefits and investigate refunds or chargebacks. These records do not make your CV public.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>12. Practical privacy choices</h2><p>Include another person's information only with a lawful basis. Remove unnecessary referee details or sensitive information before an AI request. Protect your email and password, sign out on shared devices and keep your own document backups. Guest drafts are not a permanent backup and may become unavailable after session expiry.</p><p>Deleting an account is different from cancelling a recurring payment. Stop active automatic renewals before account deletion, or email support for help. Some payment, accounting, fraud-prevention or dispute records may need to remain after deletion where lawful. Restricted backup copies may remain until their backup cycle completes; we do not promise immediate erasure from every backup or independent provider.</p><p>For access, correction, deletion, a copy of your data or a security concern, email <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>. We may verify ownership before disclosing or changing information and will explain any lawful limitation or extension.</p></section>
<section class="ats-guide-section"><h2>13. Updates and contact</h2><p>We will date revisions and give additional notice of material changes where required or appropriate. A new policy does not retrospectively authorise unrelated use of previously collected data. External services have their own notices.</p><p>Questions about storage, processing, correction, deletion or security? Contact <strong>atscvdetector</strong> at <a href="mailto:support@atscvdetector.com">support@atscvdetector.com</a>. See our <a href="{{ route('terms') }}">Terms and Conditions</a> and <a href="{{ route('refund') }}">Refund Policy</a>.</p></section>
</article>
